    "sixtySeconds": {
      "whatItDoes": "llmfit inspects your CPU, system RAM, GPUs, VRAM and accelerators and recommends open-source LLMs you can comfortably run. It ranks models by fit in an interactive terminal UI, prints tables or JSON for scripts, and can benchmark real tokens per second on your machine.",
      "problem": "It's hard to know whether a model will fit your hardware before downloading many gigabytes. llmfit answers that in one command.",
      "whoFor": [
        "People starting with local LLMs",
        "Developers choosing models for a machine",
        "Agents and scripts that need model recommendations"
      ],
      "whyChoose": "Choose it for quick, hardware-aware recommendations across hundreds of models and providers, with a TUI, JSON output, a web UI and benchmarks.",
      "requirements": [
        "Windows, macOS or Linux"
      ]
    },
    "overview": [
      "Install with winget or Scoop on Windows, Homebrew on macOS and Linux, uv tool install -U llmfit, the install script, a pre-built binary, or Docker (ghcr.io/alexsjones/llmfit).",
      "Run llmfit for the interactive TUI. Other commands: llmfit fit (ranked table), llmfit recommend --json (top picks for scripts), llmfit info <model>, llmfit bench (real tok/s against your running provider), llmfit doctor and llmfit serve (web UI and API on port 8787).",
      "You can share benchmark results to improve estimates for everyone. llmfit is MIT licensed."
